<title>USA: Koch ups U.S. posted crude oil prices 25 cts/bbl.</title>
<headline>Koch ups U.S. posted crude oil prices 25 cts/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Industries said it raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents a barrel effective Monday.</p>
<p>The increase brings the price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $17.75 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $15.00.</p>
<p>Light Lousiana sweet crude is now $17.25 and Oklahoma Sweet is $17.75.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, 212-859-1620</p>
</text>
